<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>Sentomaru.AspNetCore</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Sentomaru.AspNetCore</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>Sentomaru.AspNetCore</PackageId>
    <Version>4.11.0</Version> <!-- 4.11.0 (additive, D-25): x-sentomaru-tx-signature joins the forwarded headers, so a consumer forwards the transaction signature the app made (the server checks it only when the RFC 9421 signature covers it; no new method yet for the transaction-keys routes). Not published. 4.10.0 (additive, E-06): SentomaruTokenBinding (the hash of the user's IdP token, computed from the validated principal's sub and sid/jti), SentomaruClientOptions.TokenBindingIdpIssuer (off while null), EvaluationRequestDto.ExternalTokenBindingHash, and BindSessionAsync, RotateSessionBindingAsync and ClearSessionBindingAsync on ISentomaruClient (default 501); the token never goes to Sentomaru; a bound grant evaluated without the hash is 403 token-hardware-mismatch. Not published. 4.9.0 (additive, D-12b): IssueReattestationChallengeAsync and ReattestAsync on ISentomaruClient (default 501), ReattestationEnvelopeDto, ReattestationChallengeResponseDto and ReattestationResponseDto, and the same two methods in SentomaruEnrollmentControllerBase, so a consumer forwards the app reattest() routes as it does the enrollment (403 reattestation-disabled and reattestation-unsupported and 503 verifier-unavailable reach the app; the 429 Retry-After header is not forwarded). Not published. 4.8.0 (additive): EnrollmentTimeout (10 s by default) for the enrollment, which verifies the attestation (~1.1 s of App Attest verification on the HML server; the ExampleBackend saw it pass the 2 s Timeout, 503 store-unavailable); the enrollment waits the longer of Timeout and EnrollmentTimeout, every other call keeps Timeout, each with its own deadline under an HttpClient.Timeout of the longest plus 1 s; both capped at 5 min at startup (behaviour change: a Timeout or EnrollmentTimeout over 5 min now fails ValidateOnStart); the enrollment controller base logs the attestation reason of a refusal (short slug or "-"); codes and reasons match the slug shape up to the end of the string (\z). Not published. 4.7.0 (additive, D-17a): SentomaruEvaluationPipeline.DecideAsync (the decision of [SentomaruIntegrity] without MVC, for the gateway verifier of D-17; the attribute delegates to it, behaviour and logs unchanged), SentomaruEvaluationOptions, SentomaruDecision, SentomaruDecisionKind and SentomaruProceedReason. Not published. 4.6.0 (additive, D-06h): reattest is a known challenge kind (contract v1.10; SentomaruChallengeKinds.Reattest and Closed, SentomaruChallengeKind.Reattest after Unknown); the 401 challenge-required body carries challengeKind reattest as before; the step-up hook never runs for it (Sentomaru checks the reattestation on the next evaluation). Not published. 4.5.0 (additive, D-06b): challengeKind read from the evaluation (contract v1.9) and sent raw in the 401 challenge-required body when the policy declares one, known or not (SentomaruChallengeKind with Unknown, KnownChallengeKind, SentomaruObservation.ChallengeKind; an unknown kind such as reattest never calls the hook); optional ISentomaruChallengeHandler for step_up (ZeroTrust only; never for deny, fresh_signals, Observe nor a signed operation id; absent, refusing or throwing = 401 as 4.4.0; StepUpProceededItem after a Proceed); observedRules read. Not published. 4.4.0 (additive): SentomaruObservation (with ProofStatus; 503 integrity-unavailable when the evaluation throws, 413 body-limit) in HttpContext.Items, GetInstallationAsync (installation state), (ObservationItem) after the filter's evaluation, so a consumer filter enforces explicit installation states without a second evaluation. 4.3.0 (additive): installation-suspended (403) reaches the app on renewal/enrollment. 4.2.0 (additive): SentomaruEnrollmentControllerBase (challenge, enrollment and renewal helpers for the consumer controller). 4.1.0 (J-04r, additive): RenewSessionAsync (signed grant renewal, POST …/sessions). 4.0.0 breaking (C-09, #142): no anonymous/default caller fallback (403 caller-context-missing), AllowAnonymousContext (Development), policySource. 3.1.0: x-sentomaru-operation-id forwarded, operationId/firstAdmission, AllowOperationReplay (J-01f). 3.0.0 breaking: DeviceTrustLevel renamed DeviceAssuranceLevel -->
    <Authors>Sentomaru</Authors>
    <Company>e-bees</Company>
    <Description>ASP.NET Core adapter and action filter for Sentomaru hardware and cryptographic integrity validation.</Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/e-bees-dev/Sentomaru</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
